.TH LCD-LOCKFILE-RUNNER 1 "2026-08-11" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcd-lockfile-runner \- cycle local LCD frames from lockfiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcd-lockfile-runner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lcd-lockfile-runner
drives the local 16x2 LCD from lockfiles in the configured LCD lock
directories. It supports normal channels, generated script frames, and
temporary event frames.
.PP
Event locks preempt standby until their requested expiry. Legacy two-line
.I lcd-high
locks receive a bounded 60-second lease; add an ISO-8601 expiry on line three
when a producer requires a longer hold. The runner never redraws an unchanged
frame, avoiding flicker on a static message.
.PP
Routine "do nothing" payloads are filtered before rotation. This includes
routine/no-action generated summaries, quiet log summaries, normal power,
healthy service, and TODO/work script frames.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --lock-dir DIR
Read LCD lockfiles from
.IR DIR .
May be repeated.
.TP
.B --rotation-seconds SECONDS
Seconds to hold a normal frame.
.TP
.B --event-seconds SECONDS
Seconds to hold an event frame.
.TP
.B --once
Render one frame and exit.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the selected frame instead of writing hardware or fallback state.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfile-runner/lcd-screen.txt
Latest rendered frame.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfile-runner/lcd-history.ndjson
Rendered frame history.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/lcd-lockfile-runner/lcd-lockfile-runner.log
Runner log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lcd-system-info-publisher (1)
